<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Monarchy of the North</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1919 CE · capital Porto</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A royalist counter-revolution that restored the monarchy in northern Portugal for less than a month in 1919.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the assassination of the dictator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidonio-pais">Sidónio Pais</a> in December 1918, royalists saw an opportunity to overthrow the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-portuguese-republic">First Portuguese Republic</a>. On 19 January 1919 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henrique-paiva-couceiro">Henrique Paiva Couceiro</a> proclaimed the monarchy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> in the name of the exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-ii-of-portugal">Manuel II</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A royal governing junta ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> and much of the north, restored the blue-and-white monarchist flag and the Charter of 1826. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-ii-of-portugal">Manuel II</a>, in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, did not endorse the rising. A parallel royalist rising near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>, at Monsanto, was quickly defeated.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Republican forces, supported by armed civilians, advanced north, and a republican revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> on 13 February 1919 ended the royalist regime. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henrique-paiva-couceiro">Paiva Couceiro</a> fled to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-galicia-and-lodomeria">Galicia</a>. It was the last serious attempt to restore the Portuguese monarchy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/monarchy-of-the-north.jpg" alt="Monarchy of the North" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Tonyjeff, based on ancient national symbol. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Portugal_(1830%E2%80%931910).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1919 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Porto</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Henrique Paiva Couceiro</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Monarquia do Norte, Kingdom of the North</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=monarchy-of-the-north" aria-label="Monarchy of the North on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4470 710 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Monarchy of the North lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4790 966L4773 1045"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4773 1045h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4790 966h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4790 966h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Porto. <a href="/atlas?year=1919&amp;focus=monarchy-of-the-north">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
